<title>FRANCE: Breakdown of EU grain export/import balance.</title>
<headline>Breakdown of EU grain export/import balance.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are details of EU grain export/import commitments as of April 15 in the July-to-June 1996/97 campaign, supplied by member country officials.</p>
<p>Figures below ('000 tonnes) are based on officially communicated certificates and are subject to revision.</p>
<p>			 ---------1996/97-------  ------1995/96-----</p>
<p>			    1Jul96 to 15Apr97	1Jul95 to 15Apr96</p>
<p>			 EXPORTS  PCT(1) IMPORTS  EXPORTS    IMPORTS</p>
<p>  Soft wheat(grain)  9,579     170     893    5,620	1,204</p>
<p>  Flour (2)	    5,758     160	12    3,597	   15</p>
<p>Food aid</p>
<p>    - grain		282	67	 -	418	    -</p>
<p>    - flour (2)	  129	67	 -	192	    -</p>
<p>Donations</p>
<p>    - grain		  0		   -	335	    -</p>
<p>    - flour (2)	   17		   -	 85	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL SOFT WHEAT   15,765     154     905   10,247	1,219</p>
<p>  Durum (grain)	  120		 477	 17	1,080</p>
<p>  Semolina (3)	   315     788	 0	 40	    0</p>
<p>  Food aid		   1		   -	 72	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL DURUM WHEAT     436     338     477	129	1,080</p>
<p> ALL WHEAT	    16,201     156   1,382   10,376	2,299</p>
<p>  Barley (grain)     6,069     467	31    1,299	  205</p>
<p>  Malt (4)	     2,666     121	 0    2,197	    0</p>
<p>  Donations		  0		   -	  0	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL BARLEY	  8,735     250	31    3,496	  205</p>
<p>  Maize (grain)	  156     867   1,596	 18	2,356</p>
<p>  Food aid		  25		   -	 50	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL MAIZE	     181     266   1,596	 68	2,356</p>
<p>  Rye (grain)	    784	45	 3    1,747	   33</p>
<p>  Rye flour (5)	    4	44	 0	  9	    0</p>
<p>Donations</p>
<p>    - grain		  0		   -	 75	    -</p>
<p>    - flour (5)	    0		   -	  0	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL RYE		 788	43	 3    1,831	   33</p>
